%   data: {"dataType":"text","outputData":{"text":" <strong>linspace<\/strong> - Generate linearly spaced vector\n\n    <strong>Syntax<\/strong>\n      y = linspace(x1,x2)\n      y = linspace(x1,x2,n)\n\n    <strong>Input Arguments<\/strong>\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2026a\\help\/matlab\/ref\/double.linspace.html#bud27em-x1x2')\">x1,x2<\/a> - Point interval\n        pair of scalars\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2026a\\help\/matlab\/ref\/double.linspace.html#bud27em-n')\">n<\/a> - Number of points\n        100 (default) | real numeric scalar | NaN\n\n    <strong>Examples<\/strong>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/VectorofEvenlySpacedNumbersExample')\">Vector of Evenly Spaced Numbers<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/VectorWithSpecifiedNumberOfValuesLinspaceExample')\">Vector with Specified Number of Values<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/VectorofEvenlySpacedComplexNumbersExample')\">Vector of Evenly Spaced Complex Numbers<\/a>\n\n    <strong>See also<\/strong> <a href=\"matlab:help logspace -displayBanner\">logspace<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help colon -displayBanner\">colon<\/a>\n\n    Introduced in MATLAB before R2006a\n    <a href=\"matlab:doc linspace\">Documentation for linspace<\/a>\n    <a href=\"matlab:matlab.lang.internal.introspective.overloads.displayOverloads('linspace')\">Other uses of linspace<\/a>\n\n","truncated":false}}
